// AI layer.  AFTER sv_monsters.qc, not before: these files read its per-monster
// keys (.gag, .bloodcolor, .displayname) and QC requires a FIELD to be declared
// before use.  The other direction needs no ordering at all - sv_monsters.qc
// reaches the AI layer through forward-declared FUNCTIONS only, and touches none
// of its arrays.  All of them must stay after server/sv_navnodes.qc, which owns
// nav_pos[] and the path-slot pool.
server/sv_ai_sched.qc
server/sv_ai_anim.qc
server/sv_ai_move.qc
// Monster attack primitives.  After sv_ai_move.qc, before sv_ai_core.qc: it
// needs the AI fields and constants, and the class files below call into it.
// Faction matrix.  Before sv_ai_core.qc, which consults it on every enemy test.
server/sv_ai_factions.qc
server/sv_ai_combat.qc
server/sv_ai_core.qc
// Gibs.  After sv_ai_core.qc because choosing a gib set reads .ai_class, and
// the damage path in sv_weapons.qc (compiled far earlier) reaches Monster_Gib
// through a forward declaration.
server/sv_ai_gibs.qc
server/monsters/mon_headcrab.qc
server/monsters/mon_zombie.qc
server/monsters/mon_cockroach.qc
server/monsters/mon_islave.qc
